doc """
ConduitError controls retry behavior from within a job's perform function.

Return one of these from perform to direct what happens next:
  - Retry(msg)   — transient failure; retry with the job's configured backoff
  - Discard(msg) — permanent failure; do not retry, move to dead-letter queue
  - Snooze(dur)  — reschedule to run after the given duration (e.g. rate limits)
  - WorkerError  — unexpected worker-level error unrelated to job logic
"""

type ConduitError =
  Retry(String)
  | Discard(String)
  | Snooze(Duration)
  | WorkerError(String)
